4
00:00:05,303 --> 00:00:06,647
Nobody has published that.

5
00:00:07,052 --> 00:00:08,396
It was Figure 02.

6
00:00:08,585 --> 00:00:10,580
It picked sheet-metal parts and placed them

7
00:00:10,590 --> 00:00:13,101
on a welding fixture, in 10-hour shifts.

8
00:00:13,512 --> 00:00:14,502
According to Figure:

9
00:00:14,691 --> 00:00:19,280
more than 1,250 hours, 90,000 parts and 30,000

10
00:00:19,290 --> 00:00:19,939
cars.

11
00:00:20,368 --> 00:00:21,240
Its targets:

12
00:00:21,441 --> 00:00:25,509
84 seconds per cycle, over 99% correct cycles

13
00:00:25,521 --> 00:00:26,924
and zero interventions.

14
00:00:27,125 --> 00:00:27,927
The results?

15
00:00:28,116 --> 00:00:28,953
Not published.

16
00:00:29,372 --> 00:00:31,685
And in 2025, its founder talked about a

17
00:00:31,695 --> 00:00:32,308
fleet.

18
00:00:32,497 --> 00:00:35,082
BMW described a single robot, on a

19
00:00:35,092 --> 00:00:36,094
